[text] Review the Phase 6.2 implementation in the pointfight-reactor repository (working tree changes against HEAD = 8aaabac "phase-6.1: clip library").

Phase 6.2 ships the clip tagging UI. Acceptance criteria from docs/PHASES.md §"Phase 6.2: Clip tagging UI":
- From ClipLibraryScreen, "Tag" opens ClipTagScreen.tsx, prefilled if a prior tag exists.
- Tag screen shows `<video controls>` plus a custom scrub bar with **−1 frame** and **+1 frame** buttons (step `1/30s`).
- Cue-type select sources from CUE_LIBRARY (all 8 entries) and writes clip.cueId + clip.cueAtMs back to Dexie via an in-place update.
- Untagged clips are flagged in the library list ("needs tag") and excluded from playback in 6.3.
- Save persists; reload preserves tag.
- ClipTagScreen.test.tsx covers cue-id selection and persistence with a stubbed `<video>` element.
- Lint + tsc + vitest + vite build clean.
- Manual real-device QA documented at app/verify-phase6-2.mjs. Scrub precision is MANUAL per §B5.

Files changed / added (working tree):
- `app/src/clipmode/library.ts` — added `getClip(id)` and `updateClipTag(id, { cueId, cueAtMs })`. The latter clamps cueAtMs to [0, durationMs] and overwrites in place.
- `app/src/clipmode/library.test.ts` — +5 new tests for getClip + updateClipTag (28 tests total in this file, was 23).
- `app/src/clipmode/tag.ts` — NEW pure helpers: `FRAME_STEP_MS = 1000/30`, `stepFrame(currentMs, delta, durationMs)`, `clampCueAtMs(cueAtMs, durationMs)`.
- `app/src/clipmode/tag.test.ts` — NEW 11 unit tests covering the pure helpers.
- `app/src/ui/ClipTagScreen.tsx` — NEW. Renders `<video controls>` (blob URL from clipBlob), scrub bar (range input), ±1 frame buttons, cue-type select sourced from CUE_LIBRARY, Save button. Prefills cueId + cueAtMs from existing clip record. Lazy-loaded.
- `app/src/ui/ClipTagScreen.test.tsx` — NEW 5 component tests using @testing-library/react: cue-id selection + persistence, prefill, 8 cue options rendered, frame +/-1 ms math, close-on-missing-clip.
- `app/src/ui/ClipLibraryScreen.tsx` — added "Tag" button per row when `onTagClip` prop is provided. Wrapped Tag + Delete in `.clip-row-actions`.
- `app/src/App.tsx` — added 'tag' to IdleView union; lazy-loaded ClipTagScreen; tag view routes via taggingClipId state; Close returns to clip library.
- `app/src/App.css` — added `.clip-row-actions` and `.clip-tag-*` styles.
- `app/package.json` — added devDependencies: `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `playwright`. Project previously had no react component-test library; this is the first usage. Playwright was previously a missing dep (verify-phaseN.mjs scripts reference it).
- `app/verify-phase6-2.mjs` — NEW Playwright gate script: C1 empty-no-tag-button, C2 seeded-clip-tag-row, C3 tag-screen-renders-correctly, C4 save-persists+prefills-on-reopen. All four pass (results.json in artifacts/phase-6-2-verify/).

Verification run results:
- 236/236 vitest tests pass (was 213; +23 new: 5 library + 11 tag + 5 ClipTagScreen + 2 other library tests)
- Lint clean.
- `tsc --noEmit` clean.
- `vite build` clean. Main bundle 346.98 KB / 107.30 KB gzip (was 346.49 / 107.15 in 6.1) → delta +0.49 KB raw / +0.15 KB gzip. New ClipTagScreen chunk: 3.08 KB / 1.23 KB gzip. CSS: 13.84 / 3.28 KB (+0.95 / +0.15 KB gzip).
- verify-phase6-2.mjs: C1/C2/C3/C4 all PASS; console_errors: 0.

Review the five dimensions: correctness, readability, architecture, security, performance.

Pay particular attention to:
1. Whether updateClipTag's clamp semantics (cueAtMs ≤ durationMs) match user expectations and the §B5 video semantics (we never know the exact source FPS so 33 ms granularity may drift).
2. ClipTagScreen's effect-driven blob URL lifecycle — is revokeObjectURL guaranteed?
3. Whether the test approach (mixing pure-logic .ts test with first-time .tsx component test via @testing-library/react) introduces drift from project convention. Project previously tested all UI via verify-phaseN.mjs Playwright scripts.
4. Whether adding playwright as a devDep (previously implicit/missing) is appropriate, and whether removing the testing-library deps would have been a cleaner alternative.
5. The video element doesn't have a width/height set explicitly; CSS handles it. OK?
6. Do the data-testid hooks match the existing project pattern (kebab-case, namespaced by feature)?

Return APPROVE / REQUEST_CHANGES with concrete findings categorized as blocker / should-fix / nit. Be specific about file:line citations.
